        "possible_uses"
      ],
      "value": "Can be used to explain the biological plausibility of microbiome-mediated immune dysregulation beyond just tumor response, offering a parallel mechanism for toxicity. Helps contextualize why certain microbes are linked to organ-specific damage.",
      "role": "planning",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::ce5771d0255e802db4f7094688ef0fc074634a1308a0880d7e7de7f274e3b6aa",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "0",
            "possible_uses"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::8a4a0af034cafc40bdfbf3b7c550cfe53de2c6fc83d1b0f7e9c5afd864712d77",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::741a102037a570cf1822c524": {
      "atom_id": "atom::741a102037a570cf1822c524",
      "source_handle": "P0598",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions"
      ],
      "value": {
        "boundaries": "The review does not provide specific data on how microbiota modulation affects tumor response rates in solid tumors; its focus is on the adverse event aspect. The claim about antibiotic compromising efficacy is supported by retrospective studies cited, but the review itself does not generate new efficacy data.",
        "contribution": "Discusses the dual role of gut microbiota in influencing ICI outcomes: enhancing anti-tumor immunity (via CD8+ T cell expansion) while simultaneously increasing the risk of irAEs. It notes that antibiotic use to mitigate irAEs may compromise ICI efficacy.",
        "facet_id": "F1"
      },
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::ce5771d0255e802db4f7094688ef0fc074634a1308a0880d7e7de7f274e3b6aa",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::6346eb0fef8a85e5af8d2b30aba966b09944891dfc2dae49fbe8cf1ca3a33521",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::6f5e3c427464cfbaae581f5a": {
      "atom_id": "atom::6f5e3c427464cfbaae581f5a",
      "source_handle": "P0598",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions",
        "possible_uses"
      ],
      "value": "Useful for discussing the complex interplay between microbiota, efficacy, and toxicity. It highlights that strategies targeting the microbiome must balance these competing outcomes.",
      "role": "planning",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::ce5771d0255e802db4f7094688ef0fc074634a1308a0880d7e7de7f274e3b6aa",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "1",
            "possible_uses"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::8a4a0af034cafc40bdfbf3b7c550cfe53de2c6fc83d1b0f7e9c5afd864712d77",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::5088b14389a0aa46d2a65d4a": {
      "atom_id": "atom::5088b14389a0aa46d2a65d4a",
      "source_handle": "P0598",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "planning_summary"
      ],
      "value": "This review serves as a conceptual bridge connecting gut microbiome composition to ICI-associated myocarditis, a specific irAE. It offers mechanistic hypotheses (molecular mimicry, Treg modulation) and identifies specific microbial signatures associated with cardiac injury. While it does not directly address the modulation of ICI *efficacy* in solid tumors (its focus is on toxicity), it provides crucial context on how microbiota influences immune outcomes broadly, which may be relevant for understanding the side-effect profile of effective treatments.",
      "role": "planner_interpretation",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::ce5771d0255e802db4f7094688ef0fc074634a1308a0880d7e7de7f274e3b6aa",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "planning_summary"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::19bcfb06e7d739971ec3064cecfa0cb0b9b5c83c8ad6e930b8e85df9f22be640",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::2c5610619573e7cca590564c": {
      "atom_id": "atom::2c5610619573e7cca590564c",
      "source_handle": "P0598",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "scope_interpretation_cautions"
      ],
      "value": "The paper is a narrative review, not a systematic review or empirical study; findings represent synthesized interpretations rather than primary data.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::ce5771d0255e802db4f7094688ef0fc074634a1308a0880d7e7de7f274e3b6aa",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions",
            "0"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::7e726a58d05d0e2f08bdd5294f1df1b640b717bf2c93a5834bcb8e8c4f35955e",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::9bdf5a11c188dff9149e485d": {
      "atom_id": "atom::9bdf5a11c188dff9149e485d",
      "source_handle": "P0598",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "scope_interpretation_cautions"
      ],
      "value": "Mechanisms described (e.g., molecular mimicry, Treg suppression) are largely derived from preclinical models or extrapolated from other irAEs; direct causal evidence in human ICI-myocarditis is lacking.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::ce5771d0255e802db4f7094688ef0fc074634a1308a0880d7e7de7f274e3b6aa",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions",
            "1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::7e726a58d05d0e2f08bdd5294f1df1b640b717bf2c93a5834bcb8e8c4f35955e",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::7def4ce6d01d28e521abb86d": {
      "atom_id": "atom::7def4ce6d01d28e521abb86d",
      "source_handle": "P0598",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "scope_interpretation_cautions"
      ],
      "value": "Therapeutic suggestions (antibiotics, transplantation) are presented as future possibilities based on preclinical success; clinical application is explicitly stated as distant and controversial.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::ce5771d0255e802db4f7094688ef0fc074634a1308a0880d7e7de7f274e3b6aa",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions",
            "2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::7e726a58d05d0e2f08bdd5294f1df1b640b717bf2c93a5834bcb8e8c4f35955e",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::d67218b9052c0db3fb7408f9": {
      "atom_id": "atom::d67218b9052c0db3fb7408f9",
      "source_handle": "P0598",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "scope_interpretation_cautions"
      ],
      "value": "The review focuses on toxicity (myocarditis) rather than efficacy; do not infer conclusions about tumor response modulation from this text without caution.",
